  ('easing-holiday-stress', 220, 'Write the season''s most important dates on one calendar so nothing sneaks up on you.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 221, 'Look at the next two weeks and move one non-urgent task to after the holidays.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 222, 'Ask yourself which invitation you would be relieved to decline, and decline it.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 223, 'Choose one holiday task you''ll do imperfectly on purpose, like lopsided cookies or a messy tree.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 224, 'Tell your family which holiday activity you''re most looking forward to.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 225, 'Trade one big outing for a smaller one, like a neighborhood light walk instead of a crowded show.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 226, 'Picture the end of the season and ask what you''ll be glad you made time for.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 227, 'Write a note to go with one gift, saying why you thought of that person.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 228, 'Pay for holiday purchases with a set amount of cash or a single card, so tracking stays simple.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 229, 'Keep all your holiday receipts in one envelope or folder.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 230, 'Shop for gifts with a list in hand, and buy only what''s on it.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 231, 'Wait a full day before buying any gift that isn''t on your list.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 232, 'Set aside one evening for all your gift shopping, so it doesn''t spill across the whole season.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 233, 'Suggest a group outing instead of exchanging gifts with coworkers.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 234, 'Ask the kids to make a short wish list with three items.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 235, 'Check prices once for a big gift, choose the one that fits, and stop comparing.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 236, 'Decline an invitation by offering a different time: "I can''t this week, could we get coffee next month?"'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 237, 'Say no to hosting this year with a simple sentence: "We''re keeping things small this time."'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 238, 'Accept an invitation for just part of the event: "I''d love to stop by for dessert."'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 239, 'Decline a holiday event at work politely, if you''d rather spend that evening at home.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 240, 'Notice the urge to explain too much when declining, and send the short version instead.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 241, 'Send a kind note to someone whose event you''ll miss, wishing them a wonderful time.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 242, 'Write "rest" on your calendar the evening after each big gathering this season.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 243, 'Take a slow bath or shower the night before a busy holiday.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 244, 'Spend the hour before guests arrive doing something calm instead of last-minute cleaning.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 245, 'Lie down for ten minutes with your eyes closed between holiday commitments today.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 246, 'Plan an easy first meal for when you get home from a holiday trip, like soup in the freezer.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 247, 'Go out to the car or a porch for five minutes of quiet between holiday visits.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 248, 'Help with the dishes as a way to take a quiet break from a crowded living room.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 249, 'Step out to look at the sky or the stars for a minute during an evening celebration.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 250, 'Choose one relative you find easy to be with and sit near them at the meal.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 251, 'Imagine the touchiest moment at your next gathering and rehearse a calm reply.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 252, 'Remember that you can say "Let''s not do this today" and leave the room.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 253, 'Write a reminder card for your pocket: "I can step away. I can change the subject."'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 254, 'Before a gathering, decide what you''ll do if someone gets loud and unkind, such as taking a walk or heading home.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 255, 'Ask your partner to back you up if a certain topic comes up at the table.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 256, 'Laugh off a teasing comment once, then change the subject to something lighter.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 257, 'Set a time limit for holiday cooking, then serve what''s ready.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 258, 'Simplify the menu for your next gathering by cutting one side dish.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 259, 'Use paper plates or disposable trays for one gathering to make cleanup easier.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 260, 'Ask guests to bring their own containers for leftovers.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 261, 'Hand off the cleanup to a willing guest while you sit down with a cup of tea.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 262, 'Let someone else run the meal this time while you sit and enjoy it as a guest.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 263, 'Assign one person to keep an eye on the oven and timers while you greet guests.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 264, 'Ask a friend to help you plan a gathering so you aren''t making every decision alone.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 265, 'Ask a neighbor to bring in the mail or water plants while you''re away for the holidays.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 266, 'Arrange a ride, parking or pet care for a holiday trip at least a week ahead.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 267, 'Bring a small kindness to share on the road, like extra snacks for your travel partners.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 268, 'Use a long holiday drive to share stories, play a word game or simply ride in peace.'),
