  ('easing-holiday-stress', 270, 'Set an alert for flight or train changes so updates come to you instead of you checking.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 271, 'Wear comfortable shoes and layers on a holiday travel day so waiting is easier.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 272, 'Keep your regular wake-up time on at least a few days during the holidays.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 273, 'Have a simple breakfast before a long day of holiday errands.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 274, 'Move your body for ten minutes in the morning on a big celebration day.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 275, 'Take your usual medications or vitamins on schedule, even during holiday chaos.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 276, 'Set a gentle reminder on your phone to eat lunch on a busy holiday day.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 277, 'Leave a gathering a little early to protect your sleep before an early morning.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 278, 'Donate to a cause that someone you''ve lost cared about, in their name.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 279, 'Visit a place that you shared with someone you miss and spend a few quiet minutes there.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 280, 'Look through old holiday photos with a loved one and share memories.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 281, 'Tell your family how you''d like to honor someone who''s gone this season.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 282, 'Plan a gentle way to spend a holiday that is also the anniversary of a loss.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 283, 'Find a small way to carry on a tradition that someone you miss loved.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 284, 'Make a list of places that welcome people on holidays, like a community meal or a place of worship.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 285, 'Treat yourself to a long walk on a holiday morning when you''re on your own.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 286, 'Leave a thoughtful note for a neighbor on a holiday you''ll spend alone.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 287, 'Join an online or local group event on a holiday you''ll spend away from family.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 288, 'Tell one friend your plans for a holiday alone, so someone knows how you''re spending it and can check in.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 289, 'Send a voice message to a friend far from home, wishing them a gentle holiday.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 290, 'Create a simple ritual to mark the start of the season, like a first-snow walk or a first lantern lighting.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 291, 'Make a handwritten list of what the season means to you, and read it on a busy day.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 292, 'Choose one meaningful act of giving this season, such as helping at a food drive.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 293, 'Spend fifteen minutes this evening deciding what to leave off the holiday to-do list.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 294, 'Pick one decoration that brings you joy and put it out, and skip the rest if you like.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 295, 'Plan the season around your energy: mark which days you''re likely to be tired.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 296, 'Choose three holiday songs that make you happy and play them while you tidy.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 297, 'Make a simple dinner plan for the week of a big celebration and post it on the fridge.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 298, 'Ask a coworker how they handle the holiday rush, and share one idea of your own.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 299, 'Leave work on time on the day before a big holiday, and say so in the morning.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 300, 'Plan a lighter work schedule for the days around the big celebration.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 301, 'Put a reminder on your phone for each important holiday task so you aren''t holding it all in your head.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 302, 'Clear one surface at home before guests arrive, and let the rest stay as it is.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 303, 'Tell guests what to expect at your home: a casual meal, pajamas welcome, games after.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 304, 'Decide which room is off limits to guests so you have a calm place to retreat.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 305, 'Light a candle or put on soft music to calm the house before a gathering.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 306, 'Prepare a simple welcome for guests, like a pot of tea or a bowl of fruit, and let that be enough.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 307, 'Accept that something will go wrong at the gathering, and decide ahead of time to laugh about it.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 308, 'Ask a relative to share a recipe, and invite them to cook it with you.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 309, 'When the kitchen gets crowded, give helpers clear tasks or invite them to sit down.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 310, 'Plan a short thank-you moment at the end of a gathering to close it gently.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 311, 'Give yourself a short walk alone after the last guest leaves.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 312, 'Go to bed when you''re tired after hosting, and leave the dishes for morning.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 313, 'Ask family to share holiday photos in one place instead of everyone taking pictures all day.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 314, 'Put your phone away for one hour of a family gathering and see who you notice.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 315, 'Sit beside someone at the gathering who seems left out, and ask how their year has been.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 316, 'Take a group photo early in the gathering, then put the camera away for the rest of it.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 317, 'Offer a compliment to a relative you find hard, if you can do it honestly.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 318, 'If a relative criticizes your choices, say "Thanks, I''ve got it handled," and move on.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 319, 'Remind yourself that one hard conversation doesn''t ruin the whole holiday.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 320, 'Name one boundary you''ll keep this season, and share it with one person who''ll support you.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 321, 'Think of a relative who''s hard to be around and plan a short, friendly greeting.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 322, 'Keep your visits with difficult relatives short and pleasant.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 323, 'Plan a walk with the relative you enjoy most during a family weekend.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 324, 'Prepare a simple reply if someone presses you to have a drink, such as "I''m good with this, thanks."'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 325, 'On a cold holiday morning, bundle up and walk for fifteen minutes before the house wakes.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 326, 'On a summer holiday, find shade and a cool drink of water every hour.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 327, 'During a spring celebration, take a moment outside to notice new leaves or flowers.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 328, 'Celebrate an autumn holiday with a walk through fallen leaves before the meal.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 329, 'On a festival night, find a spot with a good view of the lights and soak it in for five minutes.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 330, 'Before a long holiday weekend, tidy your home so you return to a calm space.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 331, 'Ask yourself what you need right now, rest, food, quiet or company, on a busy holiday afternoon.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 332, 'Write down one worry about the upcoming holiday, then one small step that would ease it.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 333, 'Talk to a friend about which part of the coming season you''re dreading.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 334, 'Remind yourself that the holiday doesn''t need to be perfect to be good.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 335, 'Let go of one comparison to other families'' holidays you see online.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 336, 'Mute or unfollow accounts that make your holiday feel not good enough.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 337, 'Look back over this challenge so far, pick the to-do that helped most, and repeat it today.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 338, 'Plan a holiday-free hour: no decorating, shopping or planning, just something you enjoy.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 339, 'Read a few pages of a good book on a busy holiday evening before bed.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 340, 'Write the names of three people who make the season easier, and tell one of them.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 341, 'Take five slow breaths in the car before walking into a family gathering.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 342, 'When you arrive at a party, find the host, say hello, and then find a calm spot.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 343, 'Hold a warm cup outside in the cold air and enjoy one quiet moment of the season.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 344, 'Make a list of easy, low-cost holiday activities, like a park picnic or a movie night at home.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 345, 'Choose one free community event this season and go.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 346, 'Take a mid-afternoon tea or coffee break with your feet up on a holiday weekend.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 347, 'Hold a family meeting before the holidays to share ideas and divide jobs.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 348, 'Ask your kids how they''d like to spend the holidays, and include one of their ideas.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 349, 'Let a toddler nap at the gathering, even if it means leaving early or arriving late.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 350, 'Give kids a few minutes of warning before it''s time to leave a party.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 351, 'Keep one evening of the holiday week fully screen-free and cozy at home.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 352, 'Make a "no plans" day for the family during school break.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 353, 'Write a list of favorite holiday memories and share one at dinner.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 354, 'Choose a simple daily ritual for a holiday period, like a short gratitude walk or a nightly prayer, story or song.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 355, 'Make a small offering, wish or prayer in the way your tradition holds, and take a quiet moment with it.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 356, 'After a holiday, write a short note about one moment you want to remember.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 357, 'Sort through holiday leftovers and freeze what you''ll eat later, so nothing feels like a chore.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 358, 'Go for a walk in the first week after the holidays and enjoy the quieter streets.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 359, 'Return to your usual routines slowly after the holidays, starting with sleep.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 360, 'Return borrowed dishes and serving pieces after the season, with a quick note of thanks.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 361, 'Notice how your body feels after the holidays and choose one gentle way to care for it.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 362, 'Thank yourself for one thing you handled well this season.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 363, 'Write down three things to keep for next year and three things to change.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 364, 'Reach out to someone you lost touch with during the busy season.'),
  ('easing-holiday-stress', 365, 'Pick a date for a calm, small celebration in the quiet months, just because.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 1, 'Write one sentence that names the big change you are in right now, plainly, as if telling a kind friend.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 2, 'Pick two or three anchors to keep steady this season, such as a morning coffee, an evening walk or a Sunday call, and write them on a sticky note.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 3, 'Make two short lists side by side: what is changing in your life and what is staying the same.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 4, 'Drink a full glass of water before you check any messages this morning.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 5, 'Take a ten minute walk at the same time you usually would, even if the route is new.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 6, 'List three things you miss about the way life was before this change.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 7, 'List three things you are quietly hoping for on the other side of this change.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 8, 'Tell yourself out loud, once today, that adjusting takes time and you are allowed to be in the middle.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 9, 'Find one coffee shop, bakery or diner near where you spend most of your day and sit there for fifteen minutes.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 10, 'Put one familiar object, a mug, a photo or a blanket, somewhere you will see it first thing in the morning.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 11, 'Send a short text to someone from before the change, just to say you were thinking of them.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 12, 'Write down one practical task you could use help with this week, then name one person who might help.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 13, 'Choose the single next step on your plate and do only that step today.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 14, 'Notice one small thing that went well today in your new situation and say it to yourself.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 15, 'Eat one meal today at a table, without a screen, the way you might have before things shifted.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 16, 'Go to bed within fifteen minutes of your usual time tonight, wherever you are sleeping now.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 17, 'Name one feeling about this change that seems to contradict another one, and let both be true for a minute.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 18, 'Spend five minutes looking out a window and notice what the light is doing outside.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 19, 'Learn the name of one person you see regularly in your new routine, a neighbor, a cashier or a coworker.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 20, 'Write a note to yourself that begins, "It makes sense that this is hard because..." and finish it honestly.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 21, 'Wake up and do the same first three things you did before the change, in the same order.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 22, 'Cook or order a dish that tastes like home to you and eat it slowly.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 23, 'Look up the nearest public library and find out its hours.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 24, 'Unpack, sort or put away one box, bag or drawer, and stop there.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 25, 'Call someone who knew you before this change and ask how their week is going.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 26, 'Write down one thing you handled today that you could not have handled a few months ago.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 27, 'Pick a spot for your keys, wallet and phone and use it every time today.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 28, 'When a worry about the future comes up today, write it down and then write the one thing you can do next about it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 29, 'Stand outside for two minutes this evening and notice the temperature, the sounds and the sky.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 30, 'Hang up or prop up one picture that makes the space feel a little more like yours.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 31, 'Make a short playlist of songs that remind you of who you were before this change.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 32, 'Choose one small new routine to learn this week and write down exactly when it will happen.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 33, 'If today feels heavy, cancel or postpone one thing that is not essential and rest instead.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 34, 'Write a short goodbye note to something that has ended, a home, a job or a way of life, and keep it or tear it up.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 35, 'Take a different street on a familiar errand and notice one thing you had not seen before.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 36, 'Ask a neighbor or coworker for one local recommendation, a good park, a reliable mechanic or the best tacos.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 37, 'Set out tomorrow''s clothes tonight so the morning has one less decision in it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 38, 'Write down what a good enough day looks like during this transition, then aim for that, not a perfect one.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 39, 'Spend ten minutes in a park, courtyard or green patch near you and notice three living things.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 40, 'Give one part of your new space a job, a reading corner, a charging spot or a place for mail.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 41, 'Put a recurring reminder in your calendar to check in with one old friend every two weeks.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 42, 'Make a list of the paperwork or logistics this change has created and circle just one to handle today.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 43, 'Before you get out of bed, take three slow breaths and name one thing you can count on today.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 44, 'Notice one strength this change is asking you to use, patience, courage or flexibility, and write it down.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 45, 'Plan one simple meal you can cook on autopilot when you are tired, and buy what you need for it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 46, 'Light a candle, play soft music or open a window when you get home to mark the end of the day.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 47, 'Tell one trusted person how you are really doing with this change, in two honest sentences.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 48, 'Find the nearest place to buy groceries that you like, and walk its aisles slowly once.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 49, 'Write the date at the top of a page and describe where you are in this change today, so you can look back later.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 50, 'Choose one evening this week to be completely unscheduled and protect it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 51, 'Say no to one extra commitment today so you have room to settle.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 52, 'Keep a small notebook by your bed and write one line in it tonight about how today felt.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 53, 'Notice what time of day the change feels hardest, and plan one comforting thing for that hour tomorrow.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 54, 'Ask someone who has been through a similar change what helped them most in the first few months.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 55, 'Put on a piece of clothing you love and have had for years, and wear it today.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 56, 'Walk around your new block or building once and learn where the exits, mailboxes or bus stops are.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 57, 'Write down one thing from your old routine you want to keep and one you are glad to let go.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 58, 'Look at a photo from before this change and notice what you feel without trying to fix it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 59, 'Make your bed this morning, even loosely, so one corner of the day is already in order.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 60, 'Choose a word for this season of change, such as steady, patient or curious, and write it somewhere you will see it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 61, 'Spend fifteen minutes doing something you have always enjoyed, a puzzle, a sketch, a song, with no goal.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 62, 'If you have moved, learn how trash and recycling work in your new place and set up bins that make it easy.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 63, 'If you have started a new job, write down the names of three coworkers and one thing about each.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 64, 'If you are going through a breakup or divorce, remove or box up one item that stings to see every day.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 65, 'If there is a new baby at home, pick one ten minute task someone else could take off your hands and ask them.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 66, 'If your kids have recently left home, set a place for yourself at the table tonight and make a meal you enjoy.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 67, 'If you have recently retired, choose a regular start time for your mornings and keep it today.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 68, 'Put your phone in another room for the first twenty minutes after you wake up.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 69, 'Write a list of five things that are still exactly the same about you, no matter what has changed.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 70, 'Find out where the nearest pharmacy, urgent care and gas station are, and save them somewhere easy to find.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 71, 'Stretch your arms overhead, roll your shoulders and shake out your hands for one minute at midday.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 72, 'Thank someone who has helped you through this change so far, in a text, a call or a note.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 73, 'Look back over the last few days and circle one moment when you felt a little more at home.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 74, 'Sit down with a cup of tea and write a list of the roles you hold right now, old ones and new ones.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 75, 'Choose one chore you used to do on a set day and put it back on that same day this week.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 76, 'Visit a farmers market, flea market or street fair in your area and buy one small thing.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 77, 'Write three sentences about what you were afraid of when this change began and how it has turned out so far.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 78, 'Say yes to one offer of help today, even if you think you could manage alone.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 79, 'Make a simple map on paper of the places you now go most often, and add one you would like to try.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 80, 'Text a photo of something in your new everyday life to someone who used to share your old one.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 81, 'Set a timer for ten minutes and tidy only the surface you use most, a desk, a counter or a nightstand.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 82, 'Pick a regular wake up time for the next seven days and set one gentle alarm for it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 83, 'Eat breakfast sitting down this morning, even if it is just toast.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 84, 'When you feel unsettled today, put both feet on the floor and name five things you can see.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 85, 'Choose one evening ritual from your old life, a bath, a book or a show, and do it tonight.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 86, 'Write down three questions you still have about your new situation and who could answer each one.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 87, 'Spend a few minutes in the library browsing a shelf you would not usually visit.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 88, 'Notice one thing about your new routine that you actually like, and let yourself enjoy it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 89, 'Call or video chat with a family member and let them show you something from their day.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 90, 'Fill a small bowl or tray with things that ground you, a smooth stone, a letter, a ring, and keep it near your bed.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 91, 'Name five things you no longer have to do because of this change, and enjoy the lightness of one.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 92, 'Find out when the local trash day, street sweeping or building maintenance happens and add it to your calendar.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 93, 'Give yourself permission to feel unsure today, and write that permission on a scrap of paper.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 94, 'Take the long way home and notice how the neighborhood changes from block to block.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 95, 'Sort out one bill, account or address change that has been nagging you.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 96, 'Plan something small to look forward to this weekend, a movie, a hike or a slow breakfast.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 97, 'If a hard feeling about the change shows up today, name it in one word and let it pass without arguing.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 98, 'Wear comfortable shoes and walk to a place you have only driven past.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 99, 'Ask a friend to come over, or meet you somewhere, and help with one physical task like hanging shelves.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 100, 'Write down how long you have been in this change so far, and remind yourself that settling in usually takes longer.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 101, 'Choose one window in your home and clean it so you can see out clearly.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 102, 'Spend a few minutes reading something you loved years ago, a favorite book, a poem or an old letter.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 103, 'Learn one shortcut in your new commute, building or workplace and use it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 104, 'If you have a new boss or team, ask one person how they like to communicate and write down the answer.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 105, 'If you have moved to a new city, find the local news site or neighborhood board and read one story.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 106, 'If you lost a job, set a fixed time each day for the search and stop when it ends.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 107, 'If a family member has had a new diagnosis, write down three questions to bring to the next appointment.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 108, 'If you are caring for an aging parent, write a short list of what they still enjoy and plan one of those things.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 109, 'If you just graduated, write down three things you learned about yourself in school that will travel with you.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 110, 'Make a small plan for the hardest hour of tomorrow, and include one kind thing in it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 111, 'Take a slow shower or bath and let it be the one time today you are not solving anything.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 112, 'Stretch for five minutes before bed and loosen your jaw, shoulders and hands.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 113, 'Notice what you say to yourself when something goes wrong in the new situation, and soften one sentence.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 114, 'Find one bench, step or spot outdoors that could become a regular place to sit and breathe.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 115, 'Water a plant, or buy a small one, and give it a spot in your new routine.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 116, 'Write down three people you could call on a hard day and keep the list in your wallet or phone case.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 117, 'Choose one meal this week to share with someone, at home or out.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 118, 'Introduce yourself to one neighbor, classmate or coworker you have not met yet.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 119, 'Spend ten minutes outside in the morning light before you start your day.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 120, 'Write a short list of what you need more of right now, and one of what you need less of.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 121, 'Mark one ending with a small ritual today, such as lighting a candle, saying a few words or walking a familiar route one last time.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 122, 'Put a familiar scent in your space, a candle, a soap or a spice, that you used before the change.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 123, 'Ask yourself what would make this week ten percent easier, and do one piece of that.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 124, 'Unfollow, mute or set aside one source of news or updates that keeps stirring up the old situation.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 125, 'Make a rough budget for the next month that reflects your new situation, even if it is only five lines.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 126, 'Choose one task that feels too big and break it into three smaller steps on paper.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 127, 'Listen to a song you used to play often and notice where it takes you.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 128, 'Find a place nearby where you can hear water, birds or wind, and spend a few minutes there.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 129, 'Write one sentence to your future self, a year from now, about what you hope they will know.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 130, 'Give yourself an early night tonight, and let the dishes or email wait until morning.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 131, 'Plan your route for tomorrow''s first errand tonight so the morning feels simpler.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 132, 'Notice one moment today when you felt like yourself, and write down what you were doing.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 133, 'Try one new food, drink or dish that is common where you are now.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 134, 'Reach out to an old coworker, classmate or neighbor you have not spoken to since the change.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 135, 'Sit somewhere public, a park bench or a library table, and just let yourself be among people for a while.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 136, 'Hang a calendar or whiteboard where you can see the coming week at a glance.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 137, 'Choose one appointment you have been putting off, a doctor, a dentist or a haircut, and book it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 138, 'Before bed, list three things that went okay today, no matter how small.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 139, 'Ask someone at home how the change is going for them, and listen without fixing.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 140, 'Notice the season outside and do one thing that fits it, picking up leaves, buying a peach or watching snow.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 141, 'Put together a small comfort kit for hard days: a snack, a soft sweater, a favorite song and a phone number.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 142, 'Bring a familiar recipe into your new kitchen and cook it from start to finish.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 143, 'Find out if there is a group, class or club near you that meets around something you already love.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 144, 'Write down one thing you would tell a friend going through exactly what you are going through.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 145, 'Leave ten extra minutes for one thing today so you are not rushing through the new and unfamiliar.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 146, 'Look at your schedule for the week and cross off one thing you can drop without much loss.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 147, 'Note in your calendar the date this change began, so you can mark it gently when it comes around.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 148, 'Think of a season you went through a different change in the past, and write down one thing that got you through.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 149, 'Take a photo of your new space or setting today, so you can compare it with how it looks months from now.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 150, 'On a hard day, lower the bar: choose the three most important things and let the rest go.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 151, 'Write a list of skills you have picked up since this change started, even tiny ones like a new bus route.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 152, 'Ask a friend to remind you, in a few weeks, of something you are trying to remember about yourself right now.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 153, 'Spend a lunch break somewhere new, a plaza, a food truck or a bench by the water.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 154, 'Bring a framed photo or a small keepsake to your desk or workspace.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 155, 'Write down one tradition from before the change that you want to carry into the next holiday season.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 156, 'Hum, sing or whistle a tune from childhood while you do a chore.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 157, 'Find a quiet corner in your new library, campus or workplace that you can return to when you need a break.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 158, 'Make a short phone call to a grandparent, aunt, uncle or older friend and ask how they handled a big change.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 159, 'Pick one room or corner and arrange it the way you like, not the way it came.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 160, 'Leave a voice memo for yourself describing what today was like, and do not listen back until later.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 161, 'Plan a familiar weekend activity, pancakes, a long walk or a game night, and keep it on the calendar.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 162, 'Write the word enough at the top of a page, and list what you did today that was enough.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 163, 'Choose a small way to move your body that you can do anywhere, and do it for five minutes.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 164, 'Read the welcome papers, handbook or lease you were given and highlight one thing you did not know.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 165, 'Say thank you to someone who made your new place a little easier to live in, a landlord, a teacher or a nurse.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 166, 'Rest for twenty minutes this afternoon without guilt, lying down or sitting with your eyes closed.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 167, 'Take a walk at dusk and watch the lights come on in the windows around you.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 168, 'Set out a notebook and write one paragraph that starts with, "The hardest part right now is..."'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 169, 'Write a short paragraph that begins, "One thing that is getting easier is..." and keep it where you can reread it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 170, 'Choose a familiar breakfast and eat it at the same time three mornings in a row, starting today.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 171, 'Look for a nearby trail, river path or garden and plan a visit for your next free morning.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 172, 'If you have moved, walk to the nearest corner store or mailbox and learn the way without directions.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 173, 'If the new job comes with its own jargon, keep a running list of acronyms and terms, and add three today.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 174, 'If a long relationship has ended, plan one evening that is just for you, doing something you enjoy alone.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 175, 'If you are home with a new baby, step outside together for five minutes of fresh air.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 176, 'If your last child has moved out, send them a short message that asks nothing of them, just says hello.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 177, 'If you have retired, write a short list of things you always meant to do when you had time, and pick one.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 178, 'If you are caring for a parent, schedule one hour this week that belongs only to you and protect it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 179, 'If someone in your family has a new diagnosis, find one way to spend ordinary time together today that has nothing to do with it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 180, 'If you just finished school, set up one weekly habit that gives your week a shape, like a Monday run or a Friday call.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 181, 'Decide on one evening this week to cook a bigger batch and freeze half for a tired night.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 182, 'Look at the clutter that has piled up during this change and remove just five things from one spot.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 183, 'Find a place to sit outside on a weekend morning and drink your coffee or tea slowly.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 184, 'Write down the names of people who used to be part of your everyday life, and circle one to reach out to this week.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 185, 'When someone asks how the change is going, try giving one honest answer instead of fine.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 186, 'Make a list of what you can control this week and what you cannot, and put your energy into the first list.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 187, 'Go to bed with a book instead of a screen tonight, even for ten pages.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 188, 'Ask a coworker, neighbor or new acquaintance to join you for a short walk or a cup of coffee.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 189, 'Write down three ways you have shown up for yourself since the change began.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 190, 'Put on music while you cook dinner, and let it be a small marker that the day is winding down.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 191, 'Find one free event in your area this month, a concert, a talk or a festival, and put it on your calendar.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 192, 'Notice what your body needs right now, food, water, rest or movement, and give it one of those things.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 193, 'Look up the sunrise and sunset times where you are now and plan one walk in the daylight.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 194, 'Set aside a drawer or box for things from your old life you are not ready to decide about yet.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 195, 'Find a new route for your daily walk and give it a name of your own.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 196, 'Take stock of what is going well at work, at home or in your body, and write three short notes.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 197, 'Ask for help with one errand or chore this week, a ride, a meal or someone to watch the kids.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 198, 'Choose one thing to learn about your new place, its history, its trees or its local foods, and read about it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 199, 'Write down the first thing you want to do on the next calm weekend, and save it for then.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 200, 'Spend time today with an animal, your own pet, a neighbor''s dog or ducks at a pond.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 201, 'Sit with a mixed feeling about this change and write two columns: what I am glad about and what I am sad about.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 202, 'Close a door, literally, on one room or closet you have not finished sorting, and give yourself permission to wait.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 203, 'Leave your phone behind for a short walk, and let yourself just look around.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 204, 'Watch a movie or episode you have seen many times, just for the comfort of knowing how it ends.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 205, 'Name the anchors that have been holding you steady lately, a walk, a call or a meal, and thank yourself for keeping them.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 206, 'Write a few words about who you are becoming through this change, without needing it to be finished.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 207, 'Choose one place in your new area to visit regularly enough that someone there might start to recognize you.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 208, 'Buy or pick a few flowers and put them where you will see them every morning.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 209, 'Send a handwritten card or postcard to someone you miss, and tell them one thing about your new life.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 210, 'When you notice yourself rushing to have it all figured out, pause and ask, what is the next small thing?'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 211, 'Practice saying, "I am still getting the hang of this," in a situation where it is true.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 212, 'Spend a few minutes organizing photos from before the change into one folder or album.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 213, 'Make a short list of what you used to do for fun and choose one to try again this month.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 214, 'Stand in your doorway at the end of the day and say out loud one thing you got through.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 215, 'Clear a small surface and set something beautiful on it, a leaf, a shell or a candle.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 216, 'Write down one boundary that would protect your energy during this change, and practice it once today.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 217, 'Take a few minutes to notice the smells of your new place: the street, the kitchen, the air after rain.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 218, 'Plan a short visit to somewhere familiar from your old life, even if it is months away.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 219, 'Notice one way you are kinder to yourself now than you were at the start of this change.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 220, 'Walk into a hardware store, bookstore or garden center near you and browse for ten minutes.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 221, 'Arrange your toiletries, mugs or shoes the way you had them before, so your hands know where to reach.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 222, 'Start a running note on your phone called "Things I figured out" and add the first entry today.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 223, 'Pick one friend from before and plan a regular time to talk, the first Sunday of each month or every other Thursday.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 224, 'Ask someone you trust to handle one phone call or form you have been dreading, or to sit with you while you do it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 225, 'Practice one new routine until it feels a little smoother, like packing a lunch, catching a train or bathtime.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 226, 'When the future feels foggy, write down only what you need to do by tonight.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 227, 'Allow yourself to miss something today without deciding whether the change was right.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 228, 'Light a candle or set a flower on the table to honor something that has ended, and sit with it for a minute.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 229, 'Write three sentences about a way you have grown since this change began.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 230, 'On a rough afternoon, step away for five minutes, get some air and come back to just one task.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 231, 'Think about what this time of year meant in your old life, and choose one way to bring that into your new one.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 232, 'Notice how the light and weather where you are now differ from where you were, and write down what you like about them.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 233, 'Sit in a waiting room, lobby or park without your phone for five minutes and let your mind wander.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 234, 'Order or cook a simple soup, and eat it slowly on a quiet evening.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 235, 'Ask a librarian, barista or shop owner what they love most about the area.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 236, 'Hang a coat hook, place a doormat or set up a shoe rack so coming home feels more settled.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 237, 'Write a letter to the version of you from before the change, and tell them one thing you have learned.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 238, 'Phone a sibling, cousin or old roommate and tell them one funny thing that happened lately.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 239, 'Fold and put away one load of laundry with music on, and let it count as a small win.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 240, 'Make a list of practical questions about your new situation and email or call one office to get an answer.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 241, 'Choose one new thing to get comfortable with this week, like a commute, a schedule or a feeding time, and leave the rest for later.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 242, 'Before you start worrying about next month, write down what you need for tomorrow morning.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 243, 'Notice one thing you resent about this change and one thing you appreciate, and write both down.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 244, 'Look at an old calendar or planner and notice how much has shifted since then.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 245, 'Take a deep breath at every doorway you walk through today, as a small reset.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 246, 'Visit a park at a different time of day than usual and notice who is there.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 247, 'Pick up a takeout menu or flyer from a local spot and put it on your fridge for a tired night.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 248, 'Keep one familiar evening snack or drink in the kitchen for nights that feel off.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 249, 'Write the names of three people who would be glad to hear from you, and contact one of them.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 250, 'Ask a family member or roommate to split one recurring chore with you this week.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 251, 'Learn the name of the street, building or room you will spend the most time in tomorrow.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 252, 'Choose one decision you have been delaying and give yourself a gentle deadline for it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 253, 'Hold a cup of something warm in both hands for a minute and let your shoulders drop.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 254, 'Look up a local walking route, bike path or scenic drive and plan when you will try it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 255, 'Jot down what you are proud of carrying through this change so far.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 256, 'Spend a few minutes doing something with your hands, kneading dough, folding paper or fixing something small.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 257, 'Pause before you compare your new life with your old one, and name one thing that is simply different, not better or worse.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 258, 'Set out one thing tonight that will make tomorrow morning easier, packed bags, a filled coffee maker or ready keys.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 259, 'Visit the same coffee shop, deli or market a second time and order your new usual.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 260, 'Put a photo of people you love on your fridge, desk or bathroom mirror.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 261, 'Call a friend while you take a walk, so you have company on the move.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 262, 'If you have moved, find one local business, a barber, a bakery or a dry cleaner, and become a regular.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 263, 'If your work has changed, write down one thing you did well in your old role that you can bring to this one.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 264, 'If you are newly single, do one thing this weekend you could not do before, even something small.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 265, 'If a baby has arrived, write down one moment from today you want to remember, even a sleepy one.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 266, 'If you are adjusting to an empty house, rearrange one room so it fits the life you have now.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 267, 'If you have left your job for good, plan a weekly outing that gives you a reason to get dressed and go somewhere.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 268, 'If you help an aging parent, make a simple contact list of their doctors, neighbors and helpers and share it with one other relative.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 269, 'If a loved one is facing a health change, ask them what kind of support they would like from you this week.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 270, 'If you are starting out after school, learn one grown up task, like setting up a utility or reading a lease, and do it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 271, 'If a marriage is ending, ask a friend to help you plan one holiday or weekend so it does not catch you off guard.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 272, 'Write down what you would like this change to have taught you a year from now.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 273, 'Notice one place your body is holding tension and stretch or rub it for a minute.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 274, 'Take a few minutes to sit somewhere quiet and do nothing at all, then go back to your day.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 275, 'Plan how you will spend the next anniversary of this change, something gentle and your own.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 276, 'Let today be about one thing only, and choose it before you start.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 277, 'Write a short note to someone who is going through a change of their own, and tell them you are rooting for them.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 278, 'Find a new place to watch the sunset and go there once this week.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 279, 'Pack a small bag with things that help you feel at home, and keep it ready for long days out.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 280, 'Choose one recurring bill or account to set up automatically so there is one less thing to remember.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 281, 'Take your old routine for an afternoon, a walk, a show or a recipe, and try it in the new setting.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 282, 'Write down the one thing you are most looking forward to in the coming month.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 283, 'Make a cup of something hot, sit by a window, and let yourself feel whatever comes for five minutes.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 284, 'Ask a new acquaintance a question about themselves and really listen to the answer.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 285, 'Spend twenty minutes in a bookstore or library looking for a book about a place, hobby or skill tied to your new life.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 286, 'Write down a sound, a smell and a sight from your new days that were not part of your old ones.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 287, 'Look in the mirror this morning and say, "You are doing this," before you head out.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 288, 'Drop one expectation you have been holding about how fast you should feel settled.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 289, 'Spend a few minutes making your sleeping space calmer, dimmer lights, fewer piles or softer bedding.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 290, 'Go to a place of worship, a community center or a meeting that welcomes newcomers, and stay for a little while.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 291, 'Plan a small reward for when you finish a hard task related to this change.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 292, 'Notice how you have handled surprises in the new situation, and write down one that you met with grace.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 293, 'Find the quietest hour of your new week and plan to use it for something restful.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 294, 'On a gray or rainy day, plan one cozy thing at home, a blanket, a warm drink and a favorite show.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 295, 'In spring, plant a seed, a bulb or a pot of herbs and let it grow alongside your new routine.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 296, 'On a summer evening, sit outside after dinner and watch the light fade.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 297, 'In the fall, take a walk to look at the leaves in your new surroundings and bring one home.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 298, 'In winter, make your space warmer with one small change, an extra lamp, a throw or a pot of soup.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 299, 'Ask someone close to you what changes they have noticed in you since this began, and listen with curiosity.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 300, 'Write down how you hope to feel six months from now, and one small habit that would point toward it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 301, 'Notice when you are being hard on yourself for not adjusting faster, and say, "I am still new at this."'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 302, 'Go somewhere you have never been within twenty minutes of home and spend half an hour exploring it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 303, 'Set aside a few minutes to plan next week, writing in your anchors first and everything else after.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 304, 'Thank your body for carrying you through a demanding stretch, with a nap, a stretch or a nourishing meal.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 305, 'Make a habit of saying good morning to one person you see on your way out, and start today.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 306, 'Write a gratitude note about one thing in your old life that prepared you for this one.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 307, 'Spend part of the evening on a hobby that has nothing to do with the change.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 308, 'Sort your inbox or mailbox for ten minutes and handle only what is due this week.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 309, 'Ask someone to teach you one thing about your new role, place or situation that you have been too shy to ask.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 310, 'Find a seat near a window on a bus, train or in a cafe, and watch your new world go by for a while.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 311, 'Hold a small farewell for something from your old life, sharing a last meal, a toast or a photo with someone who was there.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 312, 'Write down one thing you used to believe about yourself that this change has proven wrong.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 313, 'Take a slow walk with no destination this afternoon and turn wherever looks interesting.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 314, 'Ask yourself, when you feel lost today, "What would steady me in the next ten minutes?" and do it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 315, 'Make tomorrow''s lunch tonight and put it somewhere easy to grab.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 316, 'Keep one evening this week for a call or visit with someone who knows your history.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 317, 'Look back over this challenge so far and pick one to-do that helped, then do it again today.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 318, 'Sort your old and new contacts, and add the people you have met recently with a note about how you met.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 319, 'Choose a small task in the new place you can master this week, like finding parking or using the laundry room.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 320, 'Say out loud, or write, one thing you are ready to stop grieving about the old life, and one thing you are not ready to stop missing.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 321, 'Give yourself a quiet half hour today to sit with how much has changed, without trying to make sense of it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 322, 'Find the closest place to get fresh air when you are inside all day, a balcony, a rooftop or a side door, and use it once.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 323, 'Share a meal or snack with a new neighbor, coworker or classmate, even something as simple as cookies.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 324, 'Write down three things you are learning to live with, and one thing you are learning to love.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 325, 'Pick one task you have been doing the old way out of habit, and test whether a new way works better here.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 326, 'Let one hard moment today be just a moment, and tell yourself that the whole day is not ruined.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 327, 'Call someone who lives in a different time zone at a time that works for both of you, and catch up.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 328, 'Bring an old ritual into a new season, like hot cocoa on the first cold night or lemonade on the first warm one.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 329, 'Make a short list of the small comforts that have helped most so far, and keep it where you can find it on a bad day.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 330, 'Go to a local event alone and stay for at least twenty minutes.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 331, 'Write down the name of the person who has surprised you most with their kindness during this change.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 332, 'Tidy your entryway so coming home feels calm instead of chaotic.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 333, 'Draw or describe your ideal ordinary day in your new life, and notice which parts already exist.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 334, 'Plan an outing to a museum, garden or landmark near you that you have been meaning to see.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 335, 'Ask a friend from your old life to send you something small from there, a photo, a snack or a note.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 336, 'Write a short list of things that are better now than before, even if the list is short.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 337, 'When you catch yourself thinking it should not be this hard, change it to, "This is hard, and I am doing it."'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 338, 'Spend a morning moving slowly, and notice what a calmer pace does for the rest of your day.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 339, 'Put your anchors on a sticky note by the door, and touch one of them before you leave home.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 340, 'Choose a familiar bedtime routine, reading, washing up and lights out, and keep it the same tonight.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 341, 'Find a regular spot at the gym, pool, park or trail where you can move your body each week.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 342, 'Offer help to someone else who is also new, a coworker, a parent at pickup or a neighbor who just moved in.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 343, 'Make peace with one unfinished task today, and set a date to come back to it.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 344, 'Write down one hope for this change that has quietly come true.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 345, 'Decide where you will turn first next time you feel overwhelmed, a person, a place or a practice, and write it down.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 346, 'Give an hour of your weekend to something that fills you up, music, cooking, gardening or a long nap.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 347, 'Take one picture each day this week of something in your new life that makes you smile, starting today.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 348, 'Plan a phone date with a parent, grandparent or old mentor and ask them about their own big changes.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 349, 'Set a kind reminder on your phone for midafternoon that says, "One step at a time."'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 350, 'Spend a few minutes noticing what has quietly become routine, and appreciate that it no longer feels new.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 351, 'Write one honest sentence about what you still find hard, and one about what you can do about it today.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 352, 'Hang or place a map of your new area somewhere you will see it, and mark the places you already know.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 353, 'Return to a spot you discovered earlier in this change and notice how it feels now that it is familiar.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 354, 'Turn down the noise for an evening: dim lights, fewer screens and quiet music.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 355, 'Revisit the list of what you miss, and notice whether anything has softened.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 356, 'Revisit your list of hopes for this change, and add one that you did not know to have at the beginning.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 357, 'Consider who you could help through a change like yours someday, and write down what you would tell them.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 358, 'Celebrate one small milestone in the new situation, the first full week, the first payday or the first friend.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 359, 'Ask someone you trust to check in on you next week, and tell them what would help.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 360, 'Make a simple plan for the next holiday or birthday that falls during this change.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 361, 'Look around your space and notice one thing that now feels like yours.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 362, 'Reread what you have written during this challenge, and notice how your words have changed.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 363, 'Write a short note of encouragement to yourself and tuck it into a coat pocket for a future day.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 364, 'Choose the two or three anchors you want to keep long after this change settles, and write why each one matters.'),
  ('steadying-yourself-through-change', 365, 'Close the day by naming one way you found steady ground today, however small.')
) as v(slug, day, task)
join public.challenge_templates t on t.slug = v.slug;
